ed cause)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute cholecystitis: less likely due to lack of fever or jaundice", "Liver abscess: possible but requires more specific imaging findings", "Exercise-induced musculoskeletal pain: contradicts hemodynamic instability", "Alcoholic hepatitis: chronic pattern mismatch with acute presentation", "Endocrine emergency (e.g., adrenal crisis): insufficient evidence of hyperglycemia or electrolyte derangements"], "alarm_features": ["Hemodynamic instability (hypotension + tachycardia)", "Peritonitis signs (diffuse tenderness, guarding)", "High-risk sexual behavior (gonococcal urethritis history)", "Recent rapid weight loss (potential malnutrition or iatrogenic risk)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Emergency with Hemorrhage Potential", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2028912675630839, "posterior": 0.3263772506593209, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["History of STI and high-risk behavior increases risk of pelvic inflammatory processes, but absence of fever/adnexal mass prevents strong support for abscess. β…"], "evidence_against": ["Classic PID signs are absent, making pelvic inflammatory disease less likely to explain RUQ pain directly."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Occlusion or Infarct", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.2889064179275193, "posterior": 0.24052078199300117, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Acute hemodynamic instability with RUQ focus is more consistent with acute vascular occlusion than chronic liver disease, but lack of cirrhosis history reduces…"], "evidence_against": ["Classic signs of chronic liver disease are absent, making vascular occlusion less likely than other acute causes of RUQ pain."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.35, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Tract Obstruction with Acute Presentation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.02842982102525069, "posterior": 0.02366843503846933, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of Murphy's sign reduces probability of common bile duct obstruction, but acute cholangitis can present without this finding."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Acute Pancreatitis / Pancreatic Inflammation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 5.5159921709009367e-05, "posterior": 1.4236524050673682e-06, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Alcohol use is a risk factor for pancreatitis, but absence of back radiation and typical acute presentation reduces likelihood of this diagnosis."], "evidence_against": ["Classic acute pancreatitis typically presents with epigastric pain radiating to back, making RUQ localization without back radiation inconsistent with this dia…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "cl